  "summary": "Overnight markets leaned dollar-strong and mildly risk-off into a quiet Treasury tape, with investors parked ahead of Fed minutes while front-end funding futures marked a sharper path. The October 2028 policy-path terminal is 4.5825 percent, up 65 basis points on the day, and cash funding is still 3.93 percent. Euro finished the 17 November fix at 1.0989, down about 2 percent over five days and at the bottom of its one-year range, with sterling at 1.3191 and broad softness in the Australian and New Zealand dollars. Dollar-yen held 159.30. Commodities split: WTI is 86.01 and Brent is 93.14, gold is 3864, and copper at 5.976 is at a seven-month low. Equities were mixed, with the Nasdaq at 24328 and the Dow at 50759, while the volatility index at 22.91 sat above complacent readings. Geopolitics stayed elevated around Hormuz and Kuwait. Macro coverage is uneven in places; these cross-asset marks are the working set. Watch euro-area inflation today, Australia jobs tomorrow, and Canada retail sales plus Japan inflation on Thursday.",
